// Shared instructions for a single admitted worker, not a Relay retry policy.
export const PROGRESS_BOUNDED_EXECUTION = `Progress-bounded execution:
Within the admitted goal, iteratively inspect evidence, diagnose failures, make bounded corrections and rerun relevant validation while each next action is justified and authorized. There is no fixed correction-count default. Repeating the same failure or action without new evidence is not progress.
Stop and preserve useful work when a human decision or additional authority is required, the next material correction is ambiguous, or no justified next action remains. Unknown prior execution state, ambiguous external mutation, uncontained prior execution, and repository, credential, security or production authority uncertainty are stop conditions.
Before every terminal return, including blocked, reconcile task-owned worktree state when safe: preserve useful changes in ordinary task commits, leave unrelated work untouched, and remove only confirmed disposable generated residue or add justified repeatable-artifact ignores without hiding useful work. Inspect actual ownership and permissions when distinguishing task work from generated residue; the worker and collector may have different access. Do not reset, blindly commit, publish, permission-repair or retry arbitrary residue. Report remaining uncommitted/non-ignored work, its known cause and the exact reconciliation or access boundary in the summary. Material execution warnings remain decision inputs for the next owner/review boundary even after a successful durable handoff. Automatic workers hand local commits to trusted Writer; this instruction grants no publication authority.
Disposable TEST state wholly inside an execution's explicitly isolated sandbox follows Relay's TEST Environment Authority (jresearchsoftware/codex-relay, docs/execution-policy.md#test-environment-authority), which scopes the generic stop, preservation and cleanup rules above.
Subagent use is discretionary and evidence-driven within the resolved Subagents permission. Select each subagent's model and reasoning effort independently based on its assignment's complexity and risk; they may differ from the parent's. By default provide a separate self-contained assignment containing its goal, necessary facts/files, constraints and completion criteria, without automatically passing full conversation or execution history. Include broader history only when materially necessary, preserving relevant prior decisions, constraints, prohibitions and protected boundaries. Delegation never expands Task/CR scope, external authority, credential access, publication or production rights. It does not authorize nested Relay workers or execution fan-out. This policy does not authorize blind Relay retries, new Relay model executions, publication, merge or deployment. Keep the admitted parent model and effort fixed and report validation truthfully.`;

